    "formula": "f(z)=frac(1,z(z-2))",
    "text": "Near a singularity, a Laurent expansion may also contain negative powers. The coefficient of one over z is called the residue at zero. For this simple pole, multiply by z and evaluate the remaining continuous factor at zero.",
