    "formula": "\"Residue at zero\"=frac(1,0-2)=-frac(1,2)",
    "text": "The residue at zero is negative one half. Around the positively oriented unit circle, zero lies inside and the other pole, two, lies outside. The residue theorem gives two pi i times the enclosed residue, hence negative pi i.",
